# This repo is public. Everything below either belongs to a client, identifies
# one, or would let someone act as this worker. Add to the patterns rather than
# naming single files: the one-file-at-a-time approach is how a confidential
# tender reached the public remote on 2026-10-09.

# Per-job working files, regenerated on every proposal
milestones.jpg
my_approach.jpg
milestones-job.html
approach-job.html

# Job queue records: contain pasted job descriptions and drafted proposals
.jobs/

# Jobs pulled off the relay before they are written. Same content as .jobs,
# one step earlier.
.queue/

# Relay threads: the server's instructions to this worker and our replies.
# Ten of these were on the public remote before being ignored here.
.threads/

# The local proposal archive. Kept out of the public repo because these carry
# client names, job descriptions and rates. Delete this line to version them.
proposals/

# Source documents that belong to other people. Clients send briefs, tenders
# and scoping documents as attachments, and they are confidential by default
# even when nothing says so. Never commit one; keep the pattern, not a list.
*.docx
*.doc
*.pdf
*.rtf
*.odt
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.csv
*.pptx
*.rar
*.zip

# Relay worker credentials. This repo is public: the token must never be in it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
proposal-bridge.json

# Editor and OS noise
.DS_Store
*.swp
*.swo
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
.idea/
.vscode/
